tasks.issue:
Feature flags that share one parameter name ignore default=True unless that flag is declared first.

    @click.option("--red", "color", flag_value="red")
    @click.option("--green", "color", flag_value="green", default=True)
    @click.option("--blue", "color", flag_value="blue")

With no arguments the value must be green, even though --red is declared first. --red still selects red.

If --red is the one with default=True and --green has no default, no arguments must yield red, and --green must yield green.

Order of declaration must not change which default wins. Only one of the flags has default=True.
